docs/program/HANDOFF.md:8:- E17 merged (PR #15, main 98eb254): 24 records, 92 in all, nine new countries (ZA, NA, EG, IL, IN, ID, JP, KR, TW); verify on the PR: 22 L1, gsq/qped blocked (403), tudelft/egg-model origin dead from the runner (data.4tu.nl timeout, also from this host). E17 findings for the planner: a `potential-fields` kind (NRCan, NAMCOR, EUG, PRIME gravity and magnetics); an access value `purchase` (BEG Stratton, NAMCOR, DGH, PASA); time-limited licences and pre-publication review (PASA). Unreached on 23 Oct: SEG (403), Kochi Core Center (503), GSJ gbank (maintenance), JAMSTEC J-CORES (reset), AOGCC (403), BRGM (refused), NRCan GDR (TLS); no data page at NUPRC, Ghana PC, Oman MEM.
docs/program/HANDOFF.md:45:E13 merged (PR #4): 42 records. E13 findings for the planner: CO2 DataShare licences carry a no-sale clause (in `notes`, no schema field); a publisher-type field would make the spread count mechanical; BRGM, NRCan GDR, CNSOER, Queensland GSQ, AOGCC, SEAM/Stratton/Viking Graben unreachable or blocked on 23 Oct (reasons in the PR body). Records slot free; no records lane chartered yet.
docs/program/HANDOFF.md:46:E03 merged (PR #7, 7ddecf0): real outlines, record/2 (`inputs`), outline/2 (`feature_id`, collection `inputs`); `osd verify --outline-inputs` in the workflow (a dispatched run now takes about 10 minutes). E04 merged (PR #8, aced173): STAC tree under site/data/stac/, offline validation with bundled schemas in `make check`, `period` optional on record/2, GeoJSON `id` = `feature_id`. E15 rebases over its two build.py edits. E16 (periods, records slot) opened. STAC address for clients: https://opensubsurfacedata.org/data/stac/catalog.json. E06 slice 1 merged (PR #9, 8b48217): `osd manifest <ids>`, `osd get <manifest> --dest`, `osd.manifest.read`; manifest/1 schema; AGENTS.md names `osd get` as a network entry point. Slice 2 (site select mode) waits for E15. E15 was the follow-up noted here (Surface, small): a build step that writes `site/data/outlines.pmtiles` from `outlines.geojson` (the E05 page already prefers it when present), so register outlines of several MB stop loading whole. E14 merged (PR #6): 68 records. E14 findings for the planner: a `microseismic` or `potential-fields` kind would admit Otway Stage 3 fibre-optic data and NRCan GDR; blocked or unreachable on 23 Oct: Mexico CNH, WAPIMS, PGI CBDG hosts, Colorado ECMC (geo-block), AOGCC, BRGM, ICDP site pages, publications.iodp.org (Zenodo deposits used instead); North Dakota DMR data is paid; Wyoming states no terms. Held back for the publisher cap: COSC-1 operational data, Northern Lights Eos thermo-mechanical set, further Ketzin sets. The open-list candidate pool is thinning: the next records lane should be chartered against a named source (one register's named datasets, or the held-back items), not another sweep.
docs/program/HANDOFF.md:47:E08 rulings (inbox note answered): CODEOWNERS names the single collaborator; GitHub teams `records-maintainers` and `kernel-maintainers` come when there are people; required code-owner review stays off, the gate stays `check`. The two outside PRs for E08's acceptance are owner evidence, owner action 101.
docs/program/HANDOFF.md:49:Codex round (OSD-D8) run on E02, E03 and E04 charters with `tools/review-charter.sh`; all three REWORK.
docs/program/HANDOFF.md:50:E02's review is dispositioned by its lane in the charter before its PR. E03 and E04 charters were
docs/program/HANDOFF.md:52:reviews stay beside them as `*-CODEX-REVIEW.md`. New decisions OSD-D11 (record versus tool
