docs/program/charters/E06-retrieval-by-manifest.md:54:them in `E06-retrieval-by-manifest-STRATEGY.md`. Where the design above and this table differ,
docs/program/charters/E06-retrieval-by-manifest.md:60:| 2.2 | Records carry more than `origin.url` | Accepted as context. The manifest reads the built catalogue, not record addresses; `manifest_url`/`inputs` stay verifier and outline inputs. |
docs/program/charters/E06-retrieval-by-manifest.md:61:| 2.3 | "No fetcher" needs qualification | Accepted. `osd get` reuses `verify.http_open`; what was missing was a manifest-driven downloader. |
docs/program/charters/E06-retrieval-by-manifest.md:62:| 2.4 | E02 `files[]` is verification output | Accepted (ruling 2). It reaches the manifest only through the STAC Collection assets; `coverage: sampled` is required whenever assets are present, and the CLI says "the files the verifier sampled, not the whole dataset". |
docs/program/charters/E06-retrieval-by-manifest.md:63:| 2.5 | Confirmed: no manifest module or `get` command | No change. |
docs/program/charters/E06-retrieval-by-manifest.md:64:| 2.6 | F3 fixture is stale (CC-BY-SA-3.0, registration, no statement) | Accepted (ruling 8). F3 is not a fixture. Attribution is tested with two supplied statements and a missing-statement case (`test_attribution_statements_verbatim`, `test_attribution_missing_statement_invents_nothing`); the real-origin transcript uses `opm/norne` and `nopims/poseidon` (anonymous, files hashed), with F3 in the same manifest showing as a registration to-do. |
docs/program/charters/E06-retrieval-by-manifest.md:67:| 3.3 | Format incomplete: version, origin, reasons | Accepted. `format: "osd.manifest/1"` (const), `origin_url`, `access`, `unresolved` required when assets are empty (schema `if/then`). |
docs/program/charters/E06-retrieval-by-manifest.md:68:| 3.4 | Rights loss | Accepted (ruling 3). The record's licence object is copied whole; absent `share_alike`/`statement` stay absent and print "not stated" / "none stated" (`test_licence_copied_whole`). |
docs/program/charters/E06-retrieval-by-manifest.md:70:| 3.6 | Unsafe resume | Accepted (ruling 5). Paths confined to `--dest/<collection_id>/`, duplicates refused before any request, temp file in the same directory, `os.replace` after size and hash match, existing files rehashed before skipping, checksum-free downloads report `fetched` (`test_rerun_repairs_truncated_and_corrupt_files`, `test_get_refuses_escaping_paths`, `test_get_without_checksum_reports_fetched`). |
docs/program/charters/E06-retrieval-by-manifest.md:72:| 3.8 | Terms enforcement undefined | Accepted (ruling 7). A restriction is carried as `licence.redistribution` plus the record's `known_issues`, verbatim; nothing is inferred from prose (`test_known_issues_and_redistribution_carried`). The stop rule above reads accordingly. |
docs/program/charters/E06-retrieval-by-manifest.md:73:| 4.1 | Schema test permits false positives | Accepted. Negative fixtures per guard: missing licence, bad checksum, format 2, userinfo, signed query, empty assets without reason, extra field, bad rights enum, climbing asset key (`test_schema_rejects[...]`). |
docs/program/charters/E06-retrieval-by-manifest.md:76:| 4.4 | Site count permits duplicates | Accepted for slice 2: the Playwright test asserts exact identities, assets, rights and reasons, with a wellbore and a Collection without Items. |
docs/program/charters/E06-retrieval-by-manifest.md:81:| 5.3 | Mirrors E07, rights mapping E09 | Accepted. The manifest preserves their inputs and implements neither. |
